%% HAND-CURATED — normalized from _seed.1 (18#L400) + plan §11 protocol_version negotiation race.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Device
    participant RealtimeService

    Device->>RealtimeService: GET /v1/realtime/connect?device_id&session_token&protocol_version=1
    alt protocol_version_unsupported
        Note over RealtimeService: server supports {1, 2} — client requested 0 or >2
        RealtimeService-->>Device: 426 protocol_version_unsupported — Retry-After-Protocol header lists supported versions
    else invalid_session_token
        Note over RealtimeService: verify JWT signature and expiry and audience
        RealtimeService-->>Device: 401 E-RT-200
    else device_inactive
        Note over RealtimeService: device decommissioned or not active
        RealtimeService-->>Device: 403 E-RT-201
    else concurrent_session_exists
        Note over RealtimeService: device already has active session
        RealtimeService-->>Device: 409 E-RT-202
    else service_at_capacity
        RealtimeService-->>Device: 503 E-RT-203
    else rate_limit_exceeded
        RealtimeService-->>Device: 429 E-RT-204
    else success
        Note over RealtimeService: verify JWT and audience and device active and household and no concurrent session
        RealtimeService-->>Device: 101 Switching Protocols (negotiated protocol_version)
        Device->>RealtimeService: SESSION_OPEN (0x01) {device_session_id, child_profile_id, interaction_mode, locale, audio_codec, sample_rate, fw_version, config_version, activation, device_timestamp_ms}
        RealtimeService-->>Device: SESSION_ACK (0x02) {session_id, max_turns=60, max_duration_ms=1800000, barge_in_enabled, cost_ceiling_usd=0.12, server_timestamp_ms}
    end
    Note over Device,RealtimeService: protocol_version negotiation race — device sends preferred version in query, server returns negotiated version in 101 — frames thereafter use negotiated version byte
